    "question": {
      ":question/id": "78641dac-e06b-5931-a04b-b1bf5b32e8e0",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
