      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+(3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{5} :={R}_{5}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
